            }
          },
          "proposition": {
            "text": "Where a mortgagor granted a permanent lease of the mortgaged property in the year 1925 and the High Court upheld the lease as against a person who had purchased the properties in a sale held in execution of a decree obtained by the mortgagee, the ground that the lease did not impair the security of the mortgagee, Held, that the lease was not binding the mortgagee or the auction purchaser as it was not a lease granted in the usual course of management, even though it did not impair the security.",
